IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pfa-powers`

-- Police Force Act 2004, ss 24 to 27, 64 and 65B -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_pfa.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`a genuine warrant obeyed` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS TRUE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS TRUE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS FALSE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS FALSE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS FALSE

`a warrant obeyed but not produced` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS FALSE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS TRUE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS FALSE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS FALSE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS FALSE

`a produced warrant not obeyed` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS TRUE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS FALSE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS FALSE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS FALSE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS FALSE

`a forged warrant signature the officer reasonably believed` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS TRUE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS TRUE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS TRUE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS FALSE

`a forged warrant-card signature the officer reasonably believed` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS TRUE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS TRUE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS TRUE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS TRUE

`a forged warrant-card signature the officer should have doubted` MEANS WarrantDefence WITH
    `the warrant was produced` IS TRUE
    `the act was proved to be done in obedience to it` IS TRUE
    `the warrant's signature is proved not genuine` IS TRUE
    `the officer reasonably believed the signature genuine` IS FALSE
    `the forged signature was on the warrant card rather than the warrant` IS TRUE

`a driver waved down who drives on` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a driver or rider`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS TRUE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a driver who misses a sign they ought to have seen` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a driver or rider`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS FALSE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a driver who stops at the barrier` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a driver or rider`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS TRUE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS TRUE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a driver who could not stop in time` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a driver or rider`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS TRUE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS TRUE

`a driver with no order and no sign` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a driver or rider`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS FALSE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a pedestrian told to stop who walks on` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a pedestrian`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS TRUE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS FALSE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a pedestrian who passes a sign only` MEANS BarrierFacts WITH
    `who` IS `a pedestrian`
    `ordered by an officer in words, a hand signal or a prescribed signal` IS FALSE
    `a warning sign was displayed that the person ought reasonably to have seen` IS TRUE
    `complied` IS FALSE
    `not reasonably practicable to do more than was done` IS FALSE

`a person on a ledge` MEANS SuicideCase WITH
    `the officer reasonably suspects an imminent or past suicide attempt` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to prevent injury or death` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary for a coroner's inquiry after a death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary to preserve evidence of an arrestable offence` IS FALSE

`a death to be inquired into` MEANS SuicideCase WITH
    `the officer reasonably suspects an imminent or past suicide attempt` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to prevent injury or death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary for a coroner's inquiry after a death` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to preserve evidence of an arrestable offence` IS FALSE

`evidence of abetment to be kept` MEANS SuicideCase WITH
    `the officer reasonably suspects an imminent or past suicide attempt` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to prevent injury or death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary for a coroner's inquiry after a death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary to preserve evidence of an arrestable offence` IS TRUE

`a suspected attempt where no power is needed` MEANS SuicideCase WITH
    `the officer reasonably suspects an imminent or past suicide attempt` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to prevent injury or death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary for a coroner's inquiry after a death` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary to preserve evidence of an arrestable offence` IS FALSE

`a burglary with no suicide` MEANS SuicideCase WITH
    `the officer reasonably suspects an imminent or past suicide attempt` IS FALSE
    `reasonably necessary to prevent injury or death` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary for a coroner's inquiry after a death` IS TRUE
    `reasonably necessary to preserve evidence of an arrestable offence` IS TRUE

`an elderly neighbour collapsed behind a locked door` MEANS EmergencyEntry WITH
    `reasonably suspects someone inside needs help through injury or ill health` IS TRUE
    `cannot get in` IS TRUE
    `entry is necessary to protect life, health or safety` IS TRUE
    `reasonably suspects a suicide attempt` IS FALSE

`the same where a suicide attempt is suspected` MEANS EmergencyEntry WITH
    `reasonably suspects someone inside needs help through injury or ill health` IS TRUE
    `cannot get in` IS TRUE
    `entry is necessary to protect life, health or safety` IS TRUE
    `reasonably suspects a suicide attempt` IS TRUE

`an unwell person whose door is open` MEANS EmergencyEntry WITH
    `reasonably suspects someone inside needs help through injury or ill health` IS TRUE
    `cannot get in` IS FALSE
    `entry is necessary to protect life, health or safety` IS TRUE
    `reasonably suspects a suicide attempt` IS FALSE

`a locked flat with no sign of need` MEANS EmergencyEntry WITH
    `reasonably suspects someone inside needs help through injury or ill health` IS FALSE
    `cannot get in` IS TRUE
    `entry is necessary to protect life, health or safety` IS FALSE
    `reasonably suspects a suicide attempt` IS FALSE

